course: dictionary
lesson: 7385
title: Words for everyday jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words are easy to understand once you see how people use them. Look at the words around the new word, and ask what job, action or thing the sentence is about. «A plumber fixes pipes, taps and toilets.» The words pipes, taps and toilets are the clues: a plumber works on water and bathroom things.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does «When a pipe leaks, you call a plumber» still make sense if you think a plumber is a person who fixes water pipes? Yes, so your meaning fits.
explain: Some phrases use words in a different way. «It'll cost an arm and a leg» does not mean anyone loses an arm or a leg. It means something is very expensive. A dictionary helps when the context does not make the meaning clear.
fact: A plumber is a person whose job is to fit and repair water pipes, taps, toilets, sinks and heating systems.
fact: You often call a plumber when a pipe leaks, a toilet is blocked or the boiler breaks.
fact: Plumbers are often self-employed, which means they work for themselves, choose their own hours and pay their own tax.
fact: «It'll cost an arm and a leg» means something is very expensive.
fact: Phrases such as call a plumber and emergency plumber are common in everyday talk.
exercise: «A plumber fixes pipes, taps and toilets.» What does a plumber mainly do? | Drives buses across the town | *Fixes water pipes, taps and toilets | Grows vegetables on a farm | Teaches children to read
exercise: When a pipe leaks at home, who would you call? | A postman | *A plumber | A pianist | A pilot
exercise: Dad sighs, «it'll cost an arm and a leg.» What does he mean? | *The job will be very expensive | The plumber has hurt his arm | The plumber cannot come at all | The job will be very cheap
test: «Plumbers are self-employed, like many plumbers and hairdressers.» What does self-employed mean? | *They work for themselves, choose their hours and pay their own tax | They work only on Sundays | They work for a big company and get a fixed wage | They never work and rely on family
test: Which problem would a plumber fix? | A cracked mirror | A lost football | *A leaking pipe | A torn page
exam: Which job would a plumber NOT do? | Mending a leaking pipe | *Painting a picture for an art gallery | Repairing a heating system | Fixing a blocked sink
